---
import DocsLayout from '../../components/DocsLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
---

<DocsLayout title="PHP" section="php">
  <h1>PHP</h1>
  <p class="lead">The Fanar PHP client sends payloads over HTTP. Call the static methods anywhere in your code — controllers, services, console commands, or jobs.</p>

  <h2>Installation</h2>
  <Code code={`composer require fanar-app/fanar`} lang="bash" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Helper function</h2>
  <p>The <code>fanar()</code> helper infers the type automatically — the same way the Node.js client does.</p>
  <Code code={`fanar('request received');              // log
fanar(['user' => $user, 'cart' => $cart]); // object — JSON tree
fanar($e);                                 // exception — stack trace

fanar($order, ['label' => 'new order', 'project' => 'shop']);`} lang="php" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Static API</h2>
  <p>Use the static methods when you need explicit control over the payload type.</p>
  <Code code={`<?php
use Fanar\\Fanar;

Fanar::log('request received');
Fanar::dump(['user' => $user, 'orders' => $orders]);
Fanar::exception($e);`} lang="php" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Methods</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Fanar::log($value)</td><td>Send a string, number, or boolean as a log entry</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Fanar::dump($value)</td><td>Send any value — rendered as a collapsible tree</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Fanar::exception($e)</td><td>Send a <code>Throwable</code> with full stack trace; origin is taken from the throw site</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>All methods accept an optional second argument for metadata:</p>
  <Code code={`Fanar::log('hello', ['label' => 'boot', 'project' => 'auth']);`} lang="php" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Named timers</h2>
  <p>Measure any block of code with a named timer. Call <code>stop()</code> to send the elapsed time to the app. Calling <code>stop()</code> more than once is safe.</p>
  <Code code={`<?php
use Fanar\\Fanar;

$t = Fanar::time('import');
importProducts($csv);
$t->stop();`} lang="php" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <p>By default the client connects to <code>localhost:23517</code>. Configure once at boot time.</p>
  <Code code={`<?php
use Fanar\\Fanar;

Fanar::configure([
  'host'    => '192.168.1.5',
  'port'    => 9913,
  'enabled' => true,
]);`} lang="php" theme="github-dark" />
</DocsLayout>
